{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"double"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDouble","text":"MXLDouble"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"<double>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"If the double element is present, it indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct\/double"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct\/double"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"double"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","text":"MXLDouble"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLTransposeV7ContentV6doubleAA9MXLDoubleVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"double","symbolKind":"property"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose/Content-swift.struct":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Content","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct","role":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose.Content","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose group represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTranspose"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTranspose"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose","role":"symbol","title":"MXLTranspose","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The transpose type represents what must be added to a written pitch to get a correct sounding pitch. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional number attribute refers to staff numbers, from top to bottom on the system. If absent, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transposition applies to all staves in the part. Per-staff transposition is most often used in parts that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"represent multiple instruments."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDouble":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldouble","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDouble"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The double type indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently written. If the above"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to yes, the doubling is one octave above what is written, as for mixed flute \/ piccolo parts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in band literature. Otherwise the doubling is one octave below what is written, as for mixed cello \/ bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parts in orchestral literature."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDouble","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDouble"}],"title":"MXLDouble"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTranspose/Content-swift.struct/double":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltranspose\/content-swift.struct\/double","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"If the double element is present, it indicates that the music is doubled one octave from what is currently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTranspose\/Content-swift.struct\/double","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"double"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDoubleV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLDouble"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"double"}}}